## Your Action Items

### Step 1: Brief Integration Agent
Send them this checklist:
- [ ] Build HCL authentication (guest session)
- [ ] Build Add to Cart action (call HCL API)
- [ ] Build Get Cart action (fetch cart state)
- [ ] Build Remove from Cart action
- [ ] Handle inventory validation
- [ ] Deploy to Adobe I/O Runtime
- [ ] Provide endpoint URLs
- [ ] Provide response JSON formats
- [ ] Test all endpoints

### Step 2: Get Response from Integration Agent
Ask for:
- [ ] Endpoint URLs (production ready)
- [ ] Request/response JSON examples
- [ ] Error format examples
- [ ] Any auth headers needed
- [ ] Rate limiting info

### Step 3: Come Back to Storefront Agent (Me)
Provide:
- Integration API endpoints
- JSON response formats
- Error handling expectations

**THEN I will build:**
- ✅ PDP Add to Cart integration
- ✅ Mini-cart updates
- ✅ Cart page display
- ✅ Error handling & feedback
- ✅ Loading states
- ✅ Full testing

---

## Key Principle

🎯 **Separation of Concerns**
- **Integration Agent = Backend/API Gateway** (HCL connectivity)
- **Storefront Agent = Frontend/UI** (User experience)
- **They communicate via REST APIs** (clean interface)

This means:
- ✅ Each agent focuses on their domain
- ✅ Changes are isolated
- ✅ Easy to test
- ✅ Scalable architecture

---

## Timeline

```
Week 1: Integration Agent builds APIs
    ↓
Week 2: Storefront Agent builds UI (using APIs)
    ↓
Week 3: End-to-end testing & refinement
    ↓
Week 4: Deploy to production
```

---

## Example: Your Exact Use Case

**Your Requirement:**
> User adds product from PDP → Check HCL → Create session → Add to HCL cart → Show in mini-cart → Show on cart page

**How We Handle It:**

```javascript
// 1. User clicks Add to Cart button on PDP
button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
  const productId = getProductIdFromPage(); // "3074457345619160265"
  const quantity = 1;
  
  // 2. Call Integration API (created by Integration Agent)
  const response = await fetch('/api/hcl/cart/add', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({ productId, quantity })
  });
  
  // 3. Integration API handles:
  //    - HCL guest login (creates session)
  //    - Check if product exists
  //    - Check inventory
  //    - Add to HCL cart
  //    - Return result
  
  if (response.ok) {
    const data = await response.json();
    // 4. Update mini-cart in header (I build this)
    updateMiniCart(data.itemCount, data.cartTotal);
    // 5. Show success message
    showSuccessMessage('Product added!');
  } else {
    // 6. Show error if HCL says product is out of stock, not found, etc.
    showErrorMessage('Product is out of stock');
  }
});

// Mini-cart display (I build this too)
async function updateMiniCart() {
  const response = await fetch('/api/hcl/cart');
  const cartData = await response.json();
  
  // Display:
  // - Item count badge
  // - Mini-cart dropdown
  // - Cart total
}
```

